### 2. 🔑 Tier 1 Trade Line Acquisition (Net-30 Vendors)

The fastest way to build credit history with a small account is to establish **Net-30 Vendor Accounts** that explicitly **report payment history** to the business credit bureaus. These are lines of credit granted by suppliers for routine business purchases, allowing you to *buy now, pay later* (typically within 30 days).

| Vendor Category | Action & Purchase Strategy | Reports To (Common) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Office/Tech Supplies** | Purchase low-cost, necessary items (paper, pens, toner, small electronics). Keep purchases modest (e.g., $50-$150) and repeat quarterly. | D&B, Experian, Equifax |
| **Industrial/Shipping** | Purchase a few basic shipping supplies or office cleaning items. These vendors are often aggressive reporters. | D&B, Experian |
| **Credit-Building Programs** | Consider low-cost membership services designed explicitly to report positive payments for credit-building (e.g., specific business fuel cards, reporting agencies). | D&B, Equifax |

**Target List for Trade Line Application (Documentation Examples):** Uline, Quill, Grainger, Staples Business Advantage.

